This is a prospective Root-only comparison adapter for the accepted R formatter
proposal a14b80e8. No Native or Rust R output has been read. The original policy
860ee62a and literal request 0aea2fae are reused byte for byte, with no added
expected text, tolerance, numerical formula, execution runner or gate update.

Invoke through the existing recorder after actual execution operands exist:
`python -X utf8 -B <compare.py> --custody <actual-packet.json>#<SHA256>
--approved-comparer-sha256 <actual-reviewed-compare.py-SHA256>
--output-dir .runtime/porting/SYS-03/<fresh-comparison-directory>`.
Root supplies real hashes; this hold supplies no future binary, outcome or ID.

The custody packet schema is `source-round-format-comparison-custody.v1`.
Its required fields are `reviewed_Source_preparation`, `Native_input`,
`Rust_input`, `observation_policy`, `Native_frozen_build_inputs`,
`Native_configure_execution`, `Native_build_execution`,
`Native_execution_build_inputs`, `Native_execution`, `Rust_build_execution`,
`Rust_execution`, `Native_execution_custody`, `Rust_execution_custody`,
`actual_Rust_sources`, `Native_provider_and_PE_evidence`,
`Root_FULL_inline_R_provider_and_PE_review_accepted` and
`Root_and_other_author_FULL_formatter_correspondence_accepted`.
Every file operand is a genuine `{path,sha256,size_bytes?}` reference.
The two review fields are actual review facts, never predicted outcomes.

Native freeze/link schemas are exactly the settled
`source-round-format-frozen-build-inputs.v1` and
`source-round-format-actual-link-inputs.v1`. They bind the full four Native
Source/input/policy rows, real additive and inherited wrappers, actual configure,
link, full binary/map and successful Original Source/core check. Inline R is
owned by actual IOFiles.hh; no imaginary noninline core provider is requested.
Root supplies genuine addr2line/PE/provider evidence as complete opaque refs.
Only the actual Native .exe/.map may reside outside the repo, on D:.

Both execution sidecars use `source-round-format-execution-custody.v1`, fields
`execution_role` (Native or Rust), `actual_command_receipt`,
`actual_input_before`, `actual_input_after`, `actual_binary_before`,
`actual_binary_after`, `input_bytes_match_before_after` and
`binary_bytes_match_before_after`. These must be real observations, not a
retroactive command guard. Native argc2 and Rust argc3 are checked exactly.
The Rust executable must come from the genuine locked CargoJSON example build.
All five Rust application rows retain `canonical_path`, `actual_literal_source`,
`actual_final_source`, `formatter_correspondence_diff`; literal proposals and
actual compiled snapshot archives are authenticated, and every diff regenerated.

All 124 owner identities, five ordered patterns and 620 exact input-bit witnesses
are required. Every nonexcluded call retains both full observations and UTF-8
text byte comparison. Only the five literal positive-infinity observations are
uninvoked Source-domain unavailable; they are fully retained and never PASS.
Missing, malformed, stopped, exception or unexpected unavailable observations
fail. Process exit0/2 must agree with actual captured call outcomes. Transport
failure emits a separate false-status record, never a valid comparison footer.

Comparison exit0 means only all 615 available selected texts match exactly;
exit1 retains all actual mismatches; exit2 records custody/shape failure. Floating
exception environment and post-nextafter NaN payload remain explicitly unpaired.
Whole declared-unit, report/backend, ordinary integration and gates stay false.
Full hash reads and end rechecks are streamed and uncapped; no producer is run.
